### Example HTML Ad:
Here is a snippet that demonstrates an ad space typically used in news sites:

```html
<div class="sidebar-advertisement" id="promo-box-300x250" data-ad-id="ad7890" data-tracking="finance-campaign" data-client="doubleclick">
 <style>
 .sidebar-advertisement { position: relative; width: 300px; height: 250px; border: 1px solid #e5e5e5; margin-top: 20px; }
 .ad-box { padding: 15px; display: inline-block; background-color: #f9f9f9; }
 .cta-link { color: #1a73e8; text-decoration: underline; font-weight: bold; }
 </style>
 <div class="ad-box">
 <img src="promo-image.jpg" alt="Get Your Offer" style="width: 280px; height: 160px; display: block;" />
 <a href="#" class="cta-link">Limited Time Finance Offer!</a>
 </div>
 <!-- Ad script loaded for DoubleClick -->
 <script type="text/javascript">
 (function() {
 window.addEventListener('load', function() {
 console.log('DoubleClick ad loaded');
 });
 window.setTimeout(() => {
 console.log('Lazy loaded for ad optimization.');
 }, 3000);
 })();
 </script>
</div>
```

### Explanation:
- The **`div`** element serves as a container with the class "sidebar-advertisement", hinting it is promotional content within the sidebar.
- The **`data-ad-id`** attribute uniquely identifies the advertisement for tracking purposes.
- The CSS styles assign position, dimensions, and aesthetics typical for news site ads.
- The embedded JavaScript mimics common dynamic ad loading practices by simulating a load event and introducing a delayed code execution to optimize display, hinting at **lazy loading strategies**.

### Classification:
- **`is_ad`: true**
- **Ad Type**: sidebar


